# Titles And Section Headers

Every post `title`, page `title`, and markdown section header (`##`, `###`) is title case. This is grammar, not shouting. Do not write SCREAMING CAPS.

Capitalize every word except the grammatical articles **a**, **an**, and **the**, unless that article is the first word of the title, the first word after a period, or the first word of a new clause that starts a line.

Prepositions, conjunctions, and verbs are capitalized: Of, For, To, On, With, And, But, Is, Does.

Deks, excerpts, and body sentences stay ordinary sentence case. This rule is titles and section heads only.

```markdown
<!-- BAD -->
title: Good luck making it home
## What notice is for
## Next door, a ballot

<!-- GOOD -->
title: Good Luck Making It Home
## What Notice Is For
## Next Door, a Ballot
```

`a` in "a Ballot" stays lowercase. `The` in "The Bill That Follows" is capitalized because it starts the line.
